  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "The final v30 text sets 24-hour reporting for all thermal incidents, a 6-year retrofit for installed units, and built-in suppression from 36 months, all within the acceptable ranges. S2 keeps identifiable per-model results confidential to regulators but gives them to buyers, with only aggregate or anonymized public release. S5 applies a mandatory 8-per-100,000 recall trigger with no transition, which would capture Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) and force a sales halt for Northwind's Hearth 10 (6.2%) under S2."
